messages.body_plain:
The problem in your program is that you declare but
never define trendError or levelError.  You need to
declare them as parameters, not transformed parameters.

Also, this

  for (t in 2:n) {
    y[t] ~ student_t(nu, l[t-1]+b[t-1], sigma);  //(nu,mu,sigma)
  }

should be much more efficient if you code it as:

  tail(y,n-1) ~ student_t(nu, head(l,n-1) + head(b,n-1), sigma);

assuming you declare y, l, and b as vectors.  (Also, using
"l" as a variable is frowned upon because it's so confusible
with "1" in many fonts.)

- Bob

